WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Two suspects are questioned
in separate rooms.

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.980
Each can confess or stay silent.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.380
Neither knows what the other will say.

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.420
Two rival firms in a cartel
face the same kind of choice:

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.860
keep to the deal, or cheat.

6
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.250
Each firm wants the most profit.

7
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.980
So how can both make their
best choice and still

8
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.630
end up worse off?

9
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.480
In this mission, you'll read
a payoff matrix and find

10
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.510
each firm's best choice.

11
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.980
Then you'll set a penalty in a graph lab,

12
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.570
and see if it can hold
the cartel together.

13
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:35.030
Your mission: find out how
two sensible choices can

14
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.910
leave both firms with less.
